From: Nerves ROCK Pi S maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] make Rockchip environment options configurable

The Radxa 2017.09 fork keeps the Rockchip environment size and offset as
non-visible Kconfig symbols, and CONFIG_ENV_OVERWRITE is still a legacy
preprocessor-only option. Expose them so Buildroot fragments can set them.
---
 env/Kconfig | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/env/Kconfig b/env/Kconfig
--- a/env/Kconfig
+++ b/env/Kconfig
@@ -441,12 +441,18 @@ config ENV_OFFSET
-	hex
+	hex "Environment offset"
 	depends on !ENV_IS_IN_UBI
 	depends on !ENV_IS_NOWHERE
 	default 0x3f8000
 	help
 	  Offset from the start of the device (or partition)
 
 config ENV_SIZE
-	hex
+	hex "Environment size"
 	default 0x8000
 	help
 	  Size of the environment storage area
+
+config ENV_OVERWRITE
+	bool "Allow board code to overwrite protected environment variables"
+	default n
+	help
+	  Permit protected variables such as serial# to be replaced.
-- 
